    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1114" xml:id="pg1114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 239</note>
                <head>No. 479<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation With Foreign
                        Secretary Eden, by the Secretary of
                        State, June 27, 1954</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d479-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-06-27">June 27,
                            1954</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I mentioned the desirability of setting up one or more informal study groups
                    which, on an unofficial basis, would consider some of the common problems of our
                    countries, where there were major divergencies of policy.</p>
                <p>Mr. Eden said he thought this matter
                    needed to be thought over and he would think it over.</p>
                <closer><signed>JFD</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
